{"as_of":"2026-09-25","company":{"ticker":"PLTR","name":"Palantir Technologies","sector":"Technology","industry":"Software","size":"large","cik":1321655},"scores":{"growth":96.0,"quality":84.0,"value":25.0,"acceleration":97.0,"price_momentum":79.0,"reality":93.0,"pricing":78.0},"strategist":{"ticker":"PLTR","opportunity_score":69.0,"components":{"structural_trend":64.0,"capital_flow":81.0,"acceleration":97.0,"quality":84.0,"valuation":25.0,"estimate_revisions":null,"management_commentary":null,"narrative_acceleration":null,"insider_institutional":null},"weights":{"structural_trend":0.2,"capital_flow":0.1,"acceleration":0.15,"quality":0.15,"valuation":0.15,"estimate_revisions":0.1,"management_commentary":0.05,"narrative_acceleration":0.05,"insider_institutional":0.05},"coverage":0.75,"unavailable":{"estimate_revisions":"Estimate-revision feed (Phase 2)","management_commentary":"Earnings Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","narrative_acceleration":"Narrative Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","insider_institutional":"Form 4 / 13F ingestion (Phase 2)"},"reality":84.0,"narrative":70.0,"pricing":70.0,"expectations_gap":15.0,"macro_fit":53.0,"sector_rotation":66.0,"theme_pricing":50.0,"checks":[{"label":"Revenue accelerating","ok":true,"evidence":"TTM growth +78.9% vs +67.7% prior quarter"},{"label":"FCF improving","ok":true,"evidence":"FCF growth +96.5%, FCF margin +54.6%"},{"label":"ROIC expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"ROIC +214.3%, incremental ROIC +500.0%"},{"label":"Margins expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"Operating margin +42.8% (+2624 bps YoY)"},{"label":"Theme exposure strengthening","ok":true,"evidence":"Exposure-weighted theme trend 64.0"},{"label":"Capital rotating toward sector","ok":true,"evidence":"Technology rotation score +66"},{"label":"Valuation below own history","ok":true,"evidence":"Cheapness vs 5y history 84.0/100"},{"label":"Valuation below sector peers","ok":false,"evidence":"Sector-relative value score 25.0"},{"label":"Balance sheet strong","ok":true,"evidence":"Net debt/EBITDA -3.5"},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":false,"evidence":"Diluted share count +1.8% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Palantir Technologies (PLTR) screens at opportunity 69.0 with an expectations gap of 15.0. Reality 84.0 reflects +78.9% TTM revenue growth, +42.8% operating margin and +214.3% ROIC; pricing 70.0 reflects a rich multiple and strong price momentum. Primary theme exposure: AI Software & Agents (trend 72.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced for sustained high growth and margin expansion; little room for disappointment.","evidence":["EV/Sales 73.6x (32.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 153x","FCF yield 0.7%","PEG 0.5","12m return +6%, -7% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (84.0) is running ahead of what is priced (70.0): an expectations gap of +15 pts."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-08-04)","AI Software & Agents: evidence that 'Trust, integration into workflows, proprietary data' is easing via Platforms owning the system of record and the data","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["Valuation leaves little room for execution slips."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 55% (currently 78.9%)","ROIC falls below 161% (currently 214.3%)","Operating margin YoY change falls below -2.0 pts (currently +26.2 pts)","Technology rotation score stays below -30 for two consecutive weeks (currently +66)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45 (currently 72.0)"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.5524,"current":0.7892},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":1.6074,"current":2.1432},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.2624472267311754},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-30,"consecutive_weeks":2,"current":66.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.9},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":26.7},{"id":"theme","label":"AI Software & Agents theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"ai-software-agents","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":72.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"ai-software-agents","theme":"AI Software & Agents","weight":0.9,"order":1,"effective":0.9},{"theme_id":"defense-modernization","theme":"Defense Modernization","weight":0.3,"order":1,"effective":0.3}],"llm":{"thesis":"Palantir is compounding at a rate that has outrun its own multiple: TTM revenue +78.9% (accelerating from +67.7%), operating margin 42.8% (+2,624bps YoY), FCF margin 54.6% and ROIC 214% \u2014 yet the stock is up only 5.5% over 12 months and trades at the 32nd percentile of its own 5-year EV/Sales range (73.6x vs a 92.7x 5y median). That combination \u2014 fundamental acceleration into multiple compression \u2014 is the core of the +15pt expectations gap (reality 84 vs pricing 70). The business is effectively capex-free ($42M capex on $6.2B revenue, 1.11x FCF conversion) with $9.4B net cash and zero debt, so incremental growth converts to cash at extraordinary rates (incremental ROIC 500%). The bull case is not multiple expansion but growth outrunning a still-extreme absolute valuation; the bear case is that at 153x earnings and a 0.7% FCF yield, a single quarter of deceleration re-rates the stock violently, and 13.6%-of-revenue SBC plus a 5% tax rate mean reported economics flatter true owner earnings.","fundamental_read":"Growth is accelerating, not decelerating \u2014 an unusual pattern at $6.2B TTM revenue \u2014 and it is accelerating alongside a 2,624bp operating-margin expansion, meaning incremental revenue is arriving at near-software-marginal cost (incremental ROIC 500%, ROE 30.9%, ROA 25.8%). Cash generation is the cleanest part of the story: $3.36B FCF on $42M capex, 54.6% FCF margin, FCF growth +96.5%, and a $9.4B net cash, zero-debt balance sheet (net debt/EBITDA -3.5) that gives full strategic optionality. The two blemishes are non-cash and structural: SBC at 13.6% of revenue with 1.8% diluted share growth, and a 5% effective tax rate that mathematically cannot persist, so GAAP net income (+295%) overstates the durable earnings base.","technical_read":"The tape is in a clean, confirmed uptrend: price 192.59 above the 20/50/200-day (178/163/152), 50>200 golden-cross structure, 26.7% above the 200-day, MACD histogram positive and RSI 67.4 \u2014 strong but not yet exhausted. The +79.5% three-month move against only +5.5% over twelve months indicates a base-and-breakout after a year-long digestion of the prior multiple, with price just 7% below the 52-week high. Key levels: the 50-day near 163 is the first structural support; a close >10% below the 200-day (~137) with negative relative strength would invalidate the trend.","market_expectation":"At 73.6x EV/Sales, 153x earnings and a 0.7% FCF yield, the market is underwriting many years of 40%+ compounding with no margin reversal and no competitive displacement \u2014 the PEG of 0.53 only looks cheap because it capitalizes an 78.9% growth rate that consensus almost certainly assumes decays hard. Simultaneously, the flat 12-month return says the market has spent a year de-rating the stock even as fundamentals improved, implying skepticism that the current growth rate is sustainable rather than an assumption that it is. In short: the multiple prices perfection over a decade, while the 12-month price action prices imminent deceleration \u2014 an internally inconsistent set of expectations.","what_market_misses":["Revenue is accelerating (+78.9% vs +67.7%) while the valuation percentile has fallen to the 32nd percentile of its own 5y range \u2014 growth has been catching up to the multiple, not the reverse, which is the mechanically bullish setup the 5.5% 12-month return obscures.","Capital intensity is near zero: $42M capex against $6.2B revenue and 1.11x FCF conversion. Unlike AI infrastructure names, Palantir captures AI demand without funding it \u2014 it is a second-order beneficiary of others' capex, not a payer.","$9.4B net cash with zero debt is not modeled as optionality: it funds acquisition, sales-capacity expansion or buybacks that could offset the 1.8% dilution without touching the P&L.","Defense Modernization exposure (weight 0.30) is a separate, budget-driven demand pool that is largely subsumed into the AI Software narrative in pricing; government program awards have different duration and cyclicality than commercial AI spend.","Incremental ROIC of 500% implies the bottleneck is go-to-market capacity, not demand or unit economics \u2014 meaning growth is a function of hiring/deployment throughput, which management can partially control."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days from the 2026-08-04 filing): a fourth consecutive quarter of revenue acceleration would force upward revision of terminal-growth assumptions.","Breakout above the 52-week high (7% away) with the 50>200 structure intact, converting the 12-month base into trend continuation.","Continued Technology sector rotation (+66, the strongest of all 11 sectors; next best Energy at +27) concentrating flows into large-cap AI software.","Evidence that the AI Software & Agents bottleneck \u2014 trust, workflow integration, proprietary data \u2014 is easing via platforms owning the system of record (theme trend 72).","Capital deployment of the $9.4B net cash position, particularly buybacks that neutralize the 1.8% annual dilution."],"risks":["0.7% FCF yield and 153x P/E leave no cushion: a deceleration to even 40-50% growth could compress the multiple far faster than earnings grow.","SBC at 13.6% of revenue and +1.8% diluted shares mean cash economics are shared with employees; on an SBC-adjusted basis the effective FCF yield is materially lower than reported.","A 5% effective tax rate is unsustainable; normalization is a mechanical hit to EPS growth that is not a business deterioration but will read as one.","Regime probabilities are effectively uniform (Goldilocks 26.6%, Contraction 25.4%, Reflation 24.6%, Stagflation 23.5%) \u2014 the 'Goldilocks' label carries little conviction, and macro fit for Technology is only 53/100.","Sector-relative valuation scores 25/100: the stock is cheap only versus its own history, expensive versus peers, so a sector-wide multiple reset hits it hardest.","Government/defense revenue concentration exposes the model to budget timing and procurement politics that do not follow commercial software cycles."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 55% (currently 78.9%) \u2014 signals the acceleration was a comp effect, not durable demand.","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY from 42.8%, indicating incremental deployments require more human capital than the software narrative assumes.","ROIC falls below ~161% or incremental ROIC collapses, showing growth is being bought rather than earned.","Diluted share count growth accelerates above ~3% or SBC exceeds ~16% of revenue without offsetting buybacks.","Price closes >10% below the 200-day average (~137) with negative relative strength.","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +66).","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45 (currently 72).","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55% (currently ~49% combined \u2014 already close)."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Cloud/compute providers and inference infrastructure: Palantir's near-zero capex means its workload growth is someone else's hosting and GPU revenue.","Systems integrators and government-cleared engineering staffing: the binding constraint on 500%-incremental-ROIC deployments is forward-deployed engineer throughput, so partners who can scale implementation capture the overflow.","FedRAMP/IL-accreditation, GovCloud and compliance-tooling vendors: every new government workload Palantir wins pulls through accredited infrastructure and security certification spend.","Data-pipeline, ETL and data-quality vendors upstream of the ontology: platforms that own the system of record still depend on clean ingestion from legacy source systems.","Data center power and cooling suppliers, as the aggregate AI-agent workload Palantir's software orchestrates lands on someone else's grid connection.","Conversely, legacy BI, custom-built government IT and on-prem analytics incumbents are the funding source \u2014 their budget lines are what Palantir's 78.9% growth is consuming."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue grew 78.9%, accelerating from 67.7% in the prior quarter.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Operating margin is 42.8%, up 2,624bps YoY; FCF margin 54.6% on $3.36B FCF with $42M capex.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Balance sheet holds $9.4B cash, zero debt, net debt/EBITDA -3.5.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"EV/Sales 73.6x sits at the 32nd percentile of the 5-year range versus a 92.7x median; P/E 153x; FCF yield 0.7%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Stock returned +5.5% over 12 months but +79.5% over 3 months; price is 26.7% above the 200-day and 7% below the 52-week high.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"SBC equals 13.6% of revenue and diluted shares grew 1.8% YoY; effective tax rate is 5%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market is pricing sustained high growth and margin expansion with little room for disappointment.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"Consensus implicitly assumes rapid decay of the current growth rate, which is why PEG reads at 0.53.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The flat 12-month return alongside accelerating fundamentals reflects multiple compression rather than business deterioration.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"A 500% incremental ROIC implies the binding constraint is deployment/go-to-market capacity rather than demand or unit economics.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Tax-rate normalization from 5% will mechanically depress EPS growth and may be misread as operational deterioration.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Defense Modernization exposure (weight 0.30) is underpriced relative to the dominant AI Software narrative.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"The $9.4B net cash position could be deployed into buybacks that offset dilution and support the multiple.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Systems integrators and cleared engineering staffing firms capture overflow demand created by Palantir's deployment bottleneck.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"}],"confidence":0.56},"llm_from":"20260925"},"technical":{"score":88,"passes":7,"criteria":{"above_150_200":true,"150_above_200":false,"200_rising_1m":true,"50_above_150_200":true,"above_50":true,"25pct_above_52w_low":true,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":true,"rs_positive_6m":true},"ready":true,"stage":"stage2_uptrend","close":192.59,"sma50":162.82,"sma150":146.93,"sma200":151.98,"sma150_prev4w":142.62,"sma150_declining":false,"pct_above_52w_low":79.5,"pct_from_52w_high":-7.0,"rs_6m":11.6,"rsi14":67.4,"atr20":7.016,"atr_pct":3.64,"overbought":false},"fundamentals":{"latest":{"period_end":"2026-06-30","filed":